    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d220">

                <pb facs="0589" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/1333</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State of a Conversation
                        with the Permian Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pezet</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">June 7, 1922</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1922-06-07">June 7, 1922</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>The Ambassador called on the Secretary at 1529 Eighteenth Street at 6.30 p.m.,
                    and said that the Peruvian Government thought that it had made a very fair
                    proposal for the arbitration of the Taena-Arica controversy; that Chile had made
                    a very unsatisfactory reply and that a deadlock had been reached; that it was
                    the understanding that the Ambassadors should respectively state their cases to
                    the Secretary. The Peruvian Ambassador had asked for an appointment because he
                    was leaving for New York, and he supposed the Chilean Ambassador would call on
                    the next day. The Ambassador left with the Secretary memoranda of what had taken
                        place,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d220-f1"/> which are annexed. The Secretary
                    made no comment, saying that he did not desire to make any suggestion until he
                    had heard from both Governments and understood fully the entire situation.</p>


                <xi:include href="d220-a1.xml" xpointer="d220-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
